---
version: 2.0.2
title: screen: settings
file: ./test/gleamdrill/snapshot_test.gleam
test_name: settings_screen_test
---
<div class="settings-screen">



  <header class="study-header">
    <h1 class="study-title">
      Settings
    </h1>
    <nav aria-label="Screens" class="study-account">
      <span class="nav-track">
        Python
      </span>
      <a class="link-button nav-link" href="/tracks">
        Tracks
      </a>
      <a class="link-button nav-link" href="/t/neetcode-150/study">
        Study
      </a>
      <a class="link-button nav-link" href="/t/neetcode-150/queue">
        Queue
      </a>
      <a class="link-button nav-link" href="/t/neetcode-150/stats">
        Stats
      </a>
      <a class="link-button nav-link" href="/tour">
        Tour
      </a>
      <span aria-current="page" class="nav-link nav-current">
        Settings
      </span>
      <span class="nav-gap"></span>
      <span class="study-email">
        drills@example.com
      </span>
      <button class="link-button nav-link">
        Sign out
      </button>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <section class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="study-section-title">
      Daily limits
    </h2>
    <p class="settings-section-note">
      Kept with your account.
    </p>
    <div class="settings-rows">
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            New problems per day
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            How many unseen problems the queue introduces. These are the expensive ones: a first encounter is read, thought about and typed from nothing.
          </span>
        </div>
        <input class="settings-input" max="100" min="0" step="1" type="number" value="5">
      </div>
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Reviews per day
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            The cap on problems already seen. A review here is minutes, not seconds, so this is a time budget wearing a card count.
          </span>
        </div>
        <input class="settings-input" max="500" min="0" step="1" type="number" value="100">
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="study-section-title">
      Scheduling
    </h2>
    <p class="settings-section-note">
      FSRS decides when a problem comes back. These change how it decides.
    </p>
    <div class="settings-rows">
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Target retention
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            The share of reviews you want to pass. Higher means shorter intervals and more work for the same material; 0.9 is the default and is a good place to stay.
          </span>
        </div>
        <input class="settings-input" max="0.99" min="0.7" step="0.01" type="number" value="0.9">
      </div>
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Day starts at
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            The hour your study day rolls over, in local time. 4am by default, so a late-night session counts toward the day it feels like rather than the one the clock says.
          </span>
        </div>
        <input class="settings-input" max="23" min="0" step="1" type="number" value="4">
      </div>
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Timezone
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            Set when you signed up. Change it if you have moved, or the day will roll over at the wrong hour.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="settings-timezone">
          <span class="settings-timezone-value">
            UTC
          </span>
          <button class="btn-secondary">
            Use this device&#39;s
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="study-section-title">
      Reminders
    </h2>
    <p class="settings-section-note">
      One plain mail on the days something is due, at the hour you pick in your timezone. Nothing on days with nothing due.
    </p>
    <div class="settings-rows">
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Daily reminder
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            Sent to drills@example.com.
          </span>
        </div>
        <select class="settings-input settings-select settings-reminder">
          <option selected value="off">
            Off
          </option>
          <option value="0">
            12 am
          </option>
          <option value="1">
            1 am
          </option>
          <option value="2">
            2 am
          </option>
          <option value="3">
            3 am
          </option>
          <option value="4">
            4 am
          </option>
          <option value="5">
            5 am
          </option>
          <option value="6">
            6 am
          </option>
          <option value="7">
            7 am
          </option>
          <option value="8">
            8 am
          </option>
          <option value="9">
            9 am
          </option>
          <option value="10">
            10 am
          </option>
          <option value="11">
            11 am
          </option>
          <option value="12">
            12 pm
          </option>
          <option value="13">
            1 pm
          </option>
          <option value="14">
            2 pm
          </option>
          <option value="15">
            3 pm
          </option>
          <option value="16">
            4 pm
          </option>
          <option value="17">
            5 pm
          </option>
          <option value="18">
            6 pm
          </option>
          <option value="19">
            7 pm
          </option>
          <option value="20">
            8 pm
          </option>
          <option value="21">
            9 pm
          </option>
          <option value="22">
            10 pm
          </option>
          <option value="23">
            11 pm
          </option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="study-section-title">
      This device
    </h2>
    <p class="settings-section-note">
      Kept in this browser, signed in or not.
    </p>
    <div class="settings-rows">
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Editor keys
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            Also switchable from the drill screen&#39;s header.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="keymap-picker">
          <button class="keymap-option active ">
            Std
          </button>
          <button class="keymap-option ">
            Vim
          </button>
          <button class="keymap-option ">
            Emacs
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Offline runtimes
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            The Gleam compiler and the Python runtime, about 11 MB, so a guest sitting runs with no network. They also fill in as you use them. Nothing cached yet.
          </span>
        </div>
        <button class="btn-secondary settings-warm" type="button">
          Download all
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="study-section-title">
      Your data
    </h2>
    <p class="settings-section-note">
      Everything your account holds, as one file. The same file restores into a guest browser, and a guest&#39;s file into an account.
    </p>
    <div class="settings-rows">
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Export study data
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            Cards, every review, settings, drafts and notes, as JSON.
          </span>
        </div>
        <button class="btn-secondary settings-export" type="button">
          Download
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="settings-row">
        <div class="settings-label">
          <span class="settings-label-text">
            Import study data
          </span>
          <span class="settings-help">
            Replaces everything here with the file&#39;s contents. You are asked first.
          </span>
        </div>
        <button class="btn-secondary settings-import" type="button">
          Choose file…
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
<div class="statusbar">
  <span class="statusbar-context">
    SETTINGS
  </span>
  <span class="leader-chip " title="Press , then a key to use a shortcut even while a button has focus">
    ,
  </span>
  <div class="statusbar-hints">
    <button class="keyhint" title="Back to study">
      <span class="keyhint-keys">
        esc/b
      </span>
      <span class="keyhint-label">
        back
      </span>
    </button>
    <button class="keyhint" title="This cheatsheet">
      <span class="keyhint-keys">
        ?
      </span>
      <span class="keyhint-label">
        keys
      </span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
<button aria-label="Help and keyboard shortcuts" class="help-fab">
  ?
</button>


